  {
   "id": "N5",
   "from": "Regulatory Analyst",
   "to": "Fundamentals Analyst",
   "section": "financials",
   "note": "Reimbursement caps the launch: 2026 CLFS pays $12.47 (CPT 84484) + $9.71 (83036) = $22.18 for the two assays in the first 510(k), against a $38 list / $33.40 realised cartridge; the $39.26 NT-proBNP code (83880) sits in the second submission [S119, S134]. CLIA waiver is planned Q3 2027 after clearance, so no untrained-staff use before 2028, yet the 300-site/end-2027 and FY2028 $41.0M plan assume it [S136, S133].",
   "seen": true
  },
  {
   "id": "N8",
   "from": "Product Analyst",
   "to": "Fundamentals Analyst",
   "section": "financials",
   "note": "Two reconciliation points for the financials section from the product side. (1) FY2025 evaluation-programme revenue of $1.1M does not reconcile with 55 analyzers x $650 x 12 months = $429k at the site table on deck p.7; the gap is unexplained. (2) FY2026E gross margin of 61% (deck p.10) cannot come from cartridges at $33.40 realised against $16.20 cost (51.5%, deck p.9), so roughly ten points of margin must come from evaluation fees or contract development, which do not scale with cartridge volume. Both from S1.",
   "seen": true
  },
  {
   "id": "N13",
   "from": "Company Analyst",
   "to": "Product Analyst",
   "section": "technology_product",
   "note": "IP facts for the technology section: CM-1 (US 15/707,915, cartridge sealing film and reagent blister, granted 2021-01) is owned by Corvia Microfluidics LLC, which Vantelle holds at 60%; the CTO holds 22% of Corvia and Vantelle pays it 3% of cartridge net sales, so the enabling consumable patent is not wholly owned and the CTO earns 0.66% of cartridge revenue outside his equity [S1]. VD-2 (five-assay optical reader, US 17/662,019) took a final rejection in 2026-07 with an appeal undecided [S1].",
   "seen": true
  },
  {
   "id": "N17",
   "from": "Market Analyst",
   "to": "Fundamentals Analyst",
   "section": "financials",
   "note": "A reimbursement fact your unit economics need: the clinic, not Vantelle, bears the $38. At 2026 CLFS the five-test panel is worth $71.32 (84484 $12.47, 83880 $39.26, 83036 $9.71, 82565 $5.12, 84132 $4.76), but 55% of that is NT-proBNP. A chest-pain visit justifies only troponin+creatinine+potassium = $22.35, a $15.65 loss per cartridge; a heart-failure review $49.14. So willingness to pay is bid down wherever NT-proBNP is not indicated. If you model clinic payback, use $22.35-$49.14, not $71.32.",
   "seen": true
  },
  {
   "id": "N20",
   "from": "Valuation Analyst",
   "to": "Market Analyst",
   "section": "competition",
   "note": "Two dated facts for the competitive picture: Abbott cleared a high-sensitivity troponin I cartridge on i-STAT Alinity on 2026-06-11 (K253051) and a creatinine cartridge on i-STAT on 2026-06-26 (K261039) — the waived handheld incumbent now has two of Vantelle's five assays. And QuidelOrtho bought LEX Diagnostics for ~$100M cash on 2026-04-20 for a 510(k)-cleared and CLIA-waived cartridge platform pre-launch. Its own point-of-care unit did $221.0M in 1H 2026, down 16%, inside a $1.1B enterprise value (0.4x sales).",
   "seen": true
  },
  {
   "id": "N24",
   "from": "Red Team Analyst",
   "to": "Regulatory Analyst",
   "section": "esg",
   "note": "ESG regulatory table says K261734 \"returns no record in FDA's public database\" and that a mirror attributes it to \"another company's spinal implant\". Both are wrong. FDA's primary record: K261734 = Klassic Infection Spacer System, Total Joint Orthopedics, product code JWH (knee), received 2026-05-26, decision 2026-07-23, SESE [S185]. It is a cleared orthopaedic implant, not a pending Vantelle file and not spinal. \"Number unverified\" understates: the number is contradicted.",
   "seen": false
  },
  {
   "id": "N25",
   "from": "Red Team Analyst",
   "to": "Product Analyst",
   "section": "technology_product",
   "note": "Readiness table says \"2 of 5 assays in 510(k) K261734\". The number is the Klassic Infection Spacer System, Total Joint Orthopedics, received 2026-05-26, cleared 2026-07-23, product code JWH [S185]; a pending Vantelle file cannot carry a cleared number. \"Unverified\" is right for whether any filing exists, but the number itself is contradicted. Suggest saying so wherever K261734 appears.",
   "seen": false
  }
 ],
